{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.JetTowerConvergence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.JetTowerConvergence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecificLimits.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecificLimits.Normed","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.InfiniteSum.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.InfiniteSum.Real"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.jet_levels_for_precision","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.jet_levels_for_precision","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jet-tower-convergence.lean#L147-L179","doc":"Engineering-facing corollary: number of jet levels needed to\nachieve binding-energy precision `ε`.\n\nThe bound `E₀ · Δmax · r^(N+1) / (1 - r) ≤ ε` becomes a log\ninequality:  `N ≥ ⌈log((ε · (1 - r)) / (E₀ · Δmax)) / log(r)⌉ - 1`.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] https://github.com/litlfred/qou ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.jet_tower_tail_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.jet_tower_tail_bound","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jet-tower-convergence.lean#L82-L145","doc":"Geometric-series tail bound for the brane-tower sum.\n\nFor any ratio `r ∈ [0, 1)`, any sequence `Δ : ℕ → ℝ` with pointwise\nbound `|Δ n| ≤ Δmax`, and any truncation point `N : ℕ`, the tail of\nthe `∑ r^(n+1) · Δ (n+1)` series is bounded by\n`Δmax · r^(N+1) / (1 - r)`.\n\nThis theorem reduces the jet-tower convergence question\n(`rem:mass-endomorphism-jet-tower` open subconjecture 1) to a\nboundedness statement on `Δ n`: once that is established, the\ngeometric series tail gives the absolute truncation error.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] https://github.com/litlfred/qou ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:jet-tower-convergence","label":"prop:jet-tower-convergence","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jet-tower-convergence.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.geometric_tail_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.geometric_tail_bound","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jet-tower-convergence.lean#L71-L80","doc":"Tail bound for the geometric series `∑_{k} r^k = r^N / (1 - r)`\nafter truncation at N. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.summable_tower_terms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.summable_tower_terms","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jet-tower-convergence.lean#L51-L69","doc":"Summability of the brane-tower term series from the comparison\nbound with a convergent geometric.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] https://github.com/litlfred/qou ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.abs_term_le_geom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.abs_term_le_geom","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jet-tower-convergence.lean#L43-L49","doc":"Comparison: `r^(n+1) * |Δ (n+1)| ≤ r^(n+1) * Δmax` when `|Δ k| ≤\nΔmax` and `r ≥ 0`.  Used for Weierstrass M-test. ","signatureChunk":0}]}